mprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T20:57:38-07:00","id":1196702,"title":"","content":"If you've been captured by terrible monsters, I don't think that you would whine about them violating your rights. They would be more likely to either beg for their lives or try to convince the Garou to let them go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T17:25:17-07:00","id":1196966,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Rage is a real curse. I imagine many introspective Garou would respond positively to someone who was honest about wanting to &quot;cure&quot; them, even if they didn't agree with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:49:03-07:00","id":1199095,"title":"","content":"but rage also causes a sense of superiority over humans RIGHTFULLY so.<br /> <br /> I dont see the garou letting them go with a slap on the wrist<br /> <br /> Saw it happen in 2 separate games and it IRKED me something feirce.<br /> <br /> I would either send them back as a spy or saboteur possibly using either Geas, or the threat of a Fetish Doll or Candle of Souls to guarantee compliance.<br /> <br /> or else.... deal with them as they deserve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T18:02:53-07:00","id":1199267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194242-how-would-dna-react-to-tables-being-turned?p=1199095#post1199095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but rage also causes a sense of superiority over humans RIGHTFULLY so.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's what cultural inculcation in the Garou Nation does. Rage just makes someone fly off the handle readily because they're basically 10,000% through with everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont see the garou letting them go with a slap on the wrist<br /> <br /> Saw it happen in 2 separate games and it IRKED me something feirce.<br /> <br /> I would either send them back as a spy or saboteur possibly using either Geas, or the threat of a Fetish Doll or Candle of Souls to guarantee compliance.<br /> <br /> or else.... deal with them as they deserve. </div> </div> </div>Countermeasures and forced double agent status are likely, but Fetish Doll is a bit limited in application and most DNA staff aren't the type that are likely to believe it works unless you use it right in front of them in a really obvious, really painful manner, which may ruin it a bit for something that you hang over a double agent's head, since you're going to be one to three levels down already. Some Shadow Lords might also dust off the Curse of the Wolf and use it on the hapless agent before letting them go &quot;free&quot;, though likely only if they're sure that the agent is going to end up collected by their handlers without delay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T04:42:16-07:00","id":1199345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194242-how-would-dna-react-to-tables-being-turned?p=1199267#post1199267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that's what cultural inculcation in the Garou Nation does. Rage just makes someone fly off the handle readily because they're basically 10,000% through with everything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Countermeasures and forced double agent status are likely, but Fetish Doll is a bit limited in application and most DNA staff aren't the type that are likely to believe it works unless you use it right in front of them in a really obvious, really painful manner, which may ruin it a bit for something that you hang over a double agent's head, since you're going to be one to three levels down already. Some Shadow Lords might also dust off the Curse of the Wolf and use it on the hapless agent before letting them go &quot;free&quot;, though likely only if they're sure that the agent is going to end up collected by their handlers without delay.</div> </div> </div> </div>On fetish Doll you can collect extra vials of blood and locks of hair and hold them for making a doll latter<br /> <br /> Hopefully, the person doesnt figure out how much trouble it is to make that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Can also use Candle of Sou's (From Hammer and klaive) To strike at a remote Target<br /> <br /> On Curse of the Wolf<br /> <br /> That would be funny!<br /> <br /> Seeing all those scientists butchered by one of their own , then for him to emerge from Frenzy covered in his friends blood.<br /> <br /> (Edit: Oh sorry Gifts name is MARK of the wolf) what do you think of Mark of the wolf forcing a Scientist to exhibit the curse for a few days would hopefull hurt their office cohesion.<br /> <br /> <br /> or maybe infallible argument of logic, giving them an unshakable belief in the holiness of the beings he was trying to &quot;Cure&quot; or would that make him not want to go back?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 03-25-2018, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T15:44:40-07:00","id":1199513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"